      "title": "Identify the loss the business faces",
      "narration": "Daniel and Elena own a repair company. They face several different problems if someone dies. An owner's family may inherit a business interest without wanting to operate the company. Losing a key manager may interrupt revenue and require a costly replacement. The company may also want to reward and retain a valuable employee. Life insurance can play a role in each situation, but the owner, beneficiary and intended use of proceeds differ. Start with the business objective. Then trace who owns the policy, whose life is insured and who receives the money.",
