      "narration": "Now suppose the company depends on Marcus, a specialist whose relationships and technical skills support important contracts. The company buys life coverage on Marcus to protect its own lawful economic interest, with the required application and consent process. The company generally owns the policy, pays the premiums and receives the covered death benefit. It may use the funds for recruiting, training, lost revenue or debt obligations. This does not automatically buy an ownership interest or pay a personal family benefit. Key-person coverage protects the business against its loss from a valuable person's death.",
